-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_colombian" id="_colombian"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.9 Colombian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_czech" id="_czech"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.10 Czech</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_english" id="_english"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.11 English</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_4dc6aeb9-1c7c-44a1-b49e-92fa5ca12d7a" id="_4dc6aeb9-1c7c-44a1-b49e-92fa5ca12d7a"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo18;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    given name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo18;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    family name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_3eb8280d-669b-4300-8d0a-d7d24f574e5a" id="_3eb8280d-669b-4300-8d0a-d7d24f574e5a"></a>English names are names used in, or originating in, England. In England as
elsewhere in the English-speaking world, a complete name usually consists of a
given name, commonly referred to as a first name or Christian name, and a (most
commonly patrilineal) family name or surname, also referred to as a last name.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_763ce4ab-738e-47b5-bd80-15fcd274bd46" id="_763ce4ab-738e-47b5-bd80-15fcd274bd46"></a>There can be several given names, some of these being often referred to as a
second name, or middle name(s).</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_2b3584d8-0b68-4506-8dfb-227fb19286fe" id="_2b3584d8-0b68-4506-8dfb-227fb19286fe"></a>Double-barrelled names, compound surnames in English feature two words,
are often joined by a hyphen or hyphens.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns" id="_typical_name_patterns"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.11.1 Typical name patterns</p>

  <p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.24</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_1e79fcd9-e847-49d2-8681-a464ccb1adb2" id="_1e79fcd9-e847-49d2-8681-a464ccb1adb2"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
<div><a name="_examples" id="_examples"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.11.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_cb935d7a-b3c2-4ff8-a2c1-d4200c2ee30c" id="_cb935d7a-b3c2-4ff8-a2c1-d4200c2ee30c"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Henry Hepburne-Scott</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ed3b30c8-13be-4e83-9520-d14638379035" id="_ed3b30c8-13be-4e83-9520-d14638379035"></a>Some families having as many as
three or four words making up their surname.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_61650a9f-3c67-4629-88da-65e41189defe" id="_61650a9f-3c67-4629-88da-65e41189defe"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Charles Hepburn-Stuart-Forbes-Trefusis, 21st Baron Clinton.</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_270b27ad-1df0-4960-bdce-b13d95249e9b" id="_270b27ad-1df0-4960-bdce-b13d95249e9b"></a>It is not unusual for compound surnames to be composed of separate words
not linked by a hyphen.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_b7d529d1-079d-452d-a93d-eecc4bdeea49" id="_b7d529d1-079d-452d-a93d-eecc4bdeea49"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></p>
  <p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.25</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_11859d9e-4fb8-45da-a440-16af34be841f" id="_11859d9e-4fb8-45da-a440-16af34be841f"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Iain</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Duncan Smith</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_french" id="_french"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.12 French</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_075cc8ee-5690-4678-9a3e-da0b654132f3" id="_075cc8ee-5690-4678-9a3e-da0b654132f3"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo19;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo19;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    given name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_319ae7bd-c3d8-45b9-be36-cf64eccad8a4" id="_319ae7bd-c3d8-45b9-be36-cf64eccad8a4"></a>French people have one, two or more given names (first names). One of them
is used in daily life.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_2" id="_typical_name_patterns_2"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.12.1 Typical name patterns</p><p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.26</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_75fd7ce6-4042-435a-b6c4-94d0417a28a0" id="_75fd7ce6-4042-435a-b6c4-94d0417a28a0"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.27</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_24502caf-cde5-446e-a178-c423f5e007ed" id="_24502caf-cde5-446e-a178-c423f5e007ed"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<div><a name="_examples_2" id="_examples_2"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.12.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_a0ac095c-9981-4656-aeaa-e0fa5985fc01" id="_a0ac095c-9981-4656-aeaa-e0fa5985fc01"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Jacques Chirac&#x201D; instead of officially of Jacques Ren&#xE9; Chirac.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_2bb5f2e5-0c34-4417-b4bf-5eeb3f66690c" id="_2bb5f2e5-0c34-4417-b4bf-5eeb3f66690c"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Philippe P&#xE9;tain&#x201D; instead of officially of Henri Philippe P&#xE9;tain,
because Philippe was the given name that he used in daily
life.</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_055b04fc-62d6-4cad-831a-4b5b225558be" id="_055b04fc-62d6-4cad-831a-4b5b225558be"></a>Middle names in the English sense do not exist, and middle initials are
never used for second or further given names.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_88b575e1-2e14-40aa-ae67-6ae1caaefebd" id="_88b575e1-2e14-40aa-ae67-6ae1caaefebd"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Claude All&#xE8;gre may be cited as &#x201C;Claude J. All&#xE8;gre&#x201D; in English-speaking
scientific publications, but not in French ones.</p></div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_german" id="_german"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.13 German</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_d1ef4d8c-fdc6-4330-9f18-de7f5e43dd50" id="_d1ef4d8c-fdc6-4330-9f18-de7f5e43dd50"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo20;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo20;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    given name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_331b6f70-903a-4c70-99d2-495a6c7f6ffa" id="_331b6f70-903a-4c70-99d2-495a6c7f6ffa"></a>Personal names in German-speaking Europe consist of one or several given names
(Vorname, plural Vornamen) and a surname (Nachname, Familienname). The Vorname
is usually gender-specific.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_3" id="_typical_name_patterns_3"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.13.1 Typical name patterns</p>

  <p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.28</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_1e8fe5e0-77e2-4483-926b-e820008669a3" id="_1e8fe5e0-77e2-4483-926b-e820008669a3"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
<div><a name="_examples_3" id="_examples_3"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.13.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_051224ad-3616-467d-8b39-5cca88aafab4" id="_051224ad-3616-467d-8b39-5cca88aafab4"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Otto Eduard Leopold F&#xFC;rst von Bismarck.</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_9c92843b-13b7-4a73-9cf1-f6ef54c2c9df" id="_9c92843b-13b7-4a73-9cf1-f6ef54c2c9df"></a>The Vorname (in English forename) is usually given to a child by the parents
shortly after birth. It is common to give a child several Vornamen (forenames).</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b02d774f-ecbb-45cc-929f-b710fe0455ff" id="_b02d774f-ecbb-45cc-929f-b710fe0455ff"></a>The Rufname (&#x201C;appellation name&#x201D; or &#x201C;call name&#x201D;) is the given name
intended for everyday use, and is often underlined on official documents.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_3f111636-c743-432c-a4ed-19967ac146ad" id="_3f111636-c743-432c-a4ed-19967ac146ad"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>The Rufname of the mathematician Amalie Emmy Noether is &#x201C;Emmy&#x201D;.</p></div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_greek" id="_greek"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.14 Greek</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_hindu" id="_hindu"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.15 Hindu</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_hungarian" id="_hungarian"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.16 Hungarian</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ed65cc47-aa98-4928-83a9-6d2f2c0c4e9f" id="_ed65cc47-aa98-4928-83a9-6d2f2c0c4e9f"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo21;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    given name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo21;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    family name
  </p>

<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_4" id="_typical_name_patterns_4"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.16.1 Typical name patterns</p>

  <p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.29</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_a9c9ac55-b9fa-4f9d-a616-7af9e11518d3" id="_a9c9ac55-b9fa-4f9d-a616-7af9e11518d3"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
<div><a name="_examples_4" id="_examples_4"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.16.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_4783fbe3-f9cd-4496-907a-9ca8fa1ae803" id="_4783fbe3-f9cd-4496-907a-9ca8fa1ae803"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Kova&#x301;cs Ja&#x301;nos</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_cc03e783-05fb-49ed-922c-49680c3cece5" id="_cc03e783-05fb-49ed-922c-49680c3cece5"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>If there is more than one given name, they come in order of importance
after the family name:</p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo22;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    Kova&#x301;cs Ja&#x301;nos Alada&#x301;r
  </p>
</div>
<div class="example"><a name="_e4b6ec5c-480c-48c9-81e0-1ec6b2e9787a" id="_e4b6ec5c-480c-48c9-81e0-1ec6b2e9787a"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>There can be more than one family name, which can be written fully or abbreviated
into initials:</p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo23;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    Segesdy Kova&#x301;cs Ja&#x301;nos
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo23;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    Segesdy-Kova&#x301;cs Ja&#x301;nos
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo23;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    S.Kova&#x301;cs Ja&#x301;nos
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo23;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    Segesdy K. Ja&#x301;nos
  </p>
</div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_icelandic" id="_icelandic"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.17 Icelandic</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_fadb1e5f-028d-4fff-b776-51d94b42d311" id="_fadb1e5f-028d-4fff-b776-51d94b42d311"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo24;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    given name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo24;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    patronymic name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo24;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    matronymic name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo24;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    genonymic name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo24;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    family name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_dae506b0-7d8b-4933-8a15-9b23f24d63e8" id="_dae506b0-7d8b-4933-8a15-9b23f24d63e8"></a>Icelandic names differ from most current Western family name systems by being
patronymic or occasionally matronymic: they indicate the father (or mother) of
the child and not the historic family lineage.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_b90c95de-ddd7-4b3a-9e87-56947fe74c83" id="_b90c95de-ddd7-4b3a-9e87-56947fe74c83"></a>Iceland&#x2019;s traditional name system was formerly used by all Nordic countries
except partly Finland.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_55131512-f67e-4c66-a673-b4b8a30295d8" id="_55131512-f67e-4c66-a673-b4b8a30295d8"></a>The Icelandic system is not based on family names
(although some people do have family names and might use both systems).
Generally, a person&#x2019;s second name indicates the first name of their father
(patronymic) or in some cases mother (matronymic). According to Icelandic
naming tradition, second names end in -son or -d&#xF3;ttir with few exceptions.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_5" id="_typical_name_patterns_5"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.17.1 Typical name patterns</p><p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.30</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_905928cd-8f7d-4bc5-88aa-1e240f314d19" id="_905928cd-8f7d-4bc5-88aa-1e240f314d19"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">patronymic or matronymic name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.31</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_f7aca97b-de24-475b-b2dc-2a45cb65e3ad" id="_f7aca97b-de24-475b-b2dc-2a45cb65e3ad"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">patronymic or matronymic name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">genonymic name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.32</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_eb8d27ef-0f8d-4770-81d5-18d81544f6d7" id="_eb8d27ef-0f8d-4770-81d5-18d81544f6d7"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">patronymic or matronymic name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">(genonymic name)</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<div><a name="_examples_5" id="_examples_5"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.17.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_267c7209-1e07-4186-a9e6-8d8d44c96fe8" id="_267c7209-1e07-4186-a9e6-8d8d44c96fe8"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>J&#xF3;hanna Sigur&#xF0;ard&#xF3;ttir. &#x201C;J&#xF3;hanna, daughter of Sigur&#xF0;ur&#x201D;.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_b4b8bf1f-75f7-4972-a4f0-d00d484be9dc" id="_b4b8bf1f-75f7-4972-a4f0-d00d484be9dc"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Matronymic. Hei&#xF0;ar Helguson, &#x201C;Helguson, son of Helga&#x201D;.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_3724343b-1e23-4953-9fe2-830759f67bb3" id="_3724343b-1e23-4953-9fe2-830759f67bb3"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#xD6;rvar &#xDE;&#xF3;reyjarson Sm&#xE1;rason. (&#xD6;rvar, son of &#xDE;&#xF3;rey, son of Sm&#xE1;ri)</p></div>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_9ef26ef8-cc12-43ac-9545-4090376df438" id="_9ef26ef8-cc12-43ac-9545-4090376df438"></a>Some family names do exist in Iceland, most commonly adaptations from last name
patronyms Icelanders took up when living abroad.</p>
<div class="example"><a name="_8636e0dd-0a06-4919-8793-1a215d33493a" id="_8636e0dd-0a06-4919-8793-1a215d33493a"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  4</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Geir Haarde, Ei&#xF0;ur Sm&#xE1;ri Gu&#xF0;johnsen, Anita Briem.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_8cef5172-92d0-4fb6-9b50-6a7f169a4038" id="_8cef5172-92d0-4fb6-9b50-6a7f169a4038"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  5</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Nobel Prize-winning author Halld&#xF3;r Laxness, born as Halld&#xF3;r Gu&#xF0;j&#xF3;nsson.</p></div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_indian" id="_indian"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.18 Indian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_indonesian" id="_indonesian"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.19 Indonesian</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_026ef364-ee7b-4cb8-a687-2b50e4052ab9" id="_026ef364-ee7b-4cb8-a687-2b50e4052ab9"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo25;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    given name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo25;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo25;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    patronymic name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ed0468f6-d8a2-46cd-9add-d30c09ff0a5c" id="_ed0468f6-d8a2-46cd-9add-d30c09ff0a5c"></a>Indonesians generally use given names without a family name.
The majority of Indonesians do not have family names. Rather,
their given names are geographically and culturally specific.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_0e269629-6752-44e8-b847-5dd95cebe015" id="_0e269629-6752-44e8-b847-5dd95cebe015"></a>Some given names include a family name or a patronymic.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_6" id="_typical_name_patterns_6"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.19.1 Typical name patterns</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_44334ac3-38f0-4f08-92c8-c45559d5061f" id="_44334ac3-38f0-4f08-92c8-c45559d5061f"></a>Indonesian names usually fall into one of the following categories:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo26;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    Mononymic names
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo26;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    Polynymic names without a family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo26;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    Polynymic names with a family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo26;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    Polynymic names with patronymic
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_6dd5452f-3d85-45e0-a88d-2caa5f60a335" id="_6dd5452f-3d85-45e0-a88d-2caa5f60a335"></a>An Indonesian name is often mis-represented in other cultures, such as:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo27;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    Netherlands: the word &#x201C;Onbekend&#x201D; (&#x201C;unknown&#x201D;) is assigned as a last name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo27;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    Germany: the one-word name is used as both given name and surname
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo27;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    US: &#x201C;Fnu&#x201D; (family name unknown) is assigned as the first or given name, &#x201C;Lnu&#x201D; (last name unknown) is assigned as the family, surname or last name,
or the name is duplicated as the surname.
  </p>
</div>
<div><a name="_examples_6" id="_examples_6"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.19.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_56ff4788-5bbc-47a5-bc62-7b0c34d37090" id="_56ff4788-5bbc-47a5-bc62-7b0c34d37090"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;Mulyono&#x201D;, the original name of &#x201C;Joko Widodo&#x201D;</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_5b6252a3-d99b-4d82-987d-7e55958f5592" id="_5b6252a3-d99b-4d82-987d-7e55958f5592"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Kusno Sosrodihardjo</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_a9df8401-168a-4d40-ab3d-d0d738ab83c4" id="_a9df8401-168a-4d40-ab3d-d0d738ab83c4"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Fransiskus Xaverius Hadi Rudyatmo</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_d1e55708-78b7-47dc-b62d-b8b184c5648a" id="_d1e55708-78b7-47dc-b62d-b8b184c5648a"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  4</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>Sudono Salim</p></div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_iranian" id="_iranian"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.20 Iranian</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_iraqi" id="_iraqi"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.21 Iraqi</p>

</div>
        <div><a name="_italian" id="_italian"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.22 Italian</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_d8a7ba94-4849-410f-848f-36e1e05dc219" id="_d8a7ba94-4849-410f-848f-36e1e05dc219"></a>A name in Italian consists of a given name (nome) and a surname (cognome).
Surnames are normally written after given names.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_044a67b9-69d3-43de-bfe6-b8438368859f" id="_044a67b9-69d3-43de-bfe6-b8438368859f"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo28;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo28;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    given name
  </p>
</div>
        <div><a name="_japanese" id="_japanese"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.23 Japanese</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_ae0aa723-aab6-4174-8f3b-1390d056f83c" id="_ae0aa723-aab6-4174-8f3b-1390d056f83c"></a>Japanese names usually consist of a family name (surname),
followed by a given name.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_e2096e27-bd31-44ce-b8a2-376c8191c2f9" id="_e2096e27-bd31-44ce-b8a2-376c8191c2f9"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo29;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo29;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    given name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_139d384e-e05d-415e-b1b5-b24547845671" id="_139d384e-e05d-415e-b1b5-b24547845671"></a>Japanese names are usually written in kanji,
where characters are logographic, but each with a variety of
possible Japanese pronunciations.
Therefore, names often cannot be spelled or pronounced
unless both the spelling and pronunciation are given.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_7" id="_typical_name_patterns_7"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.23.1 Typical name patterns</p>

  <p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.33</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_110c320b-db48-4ed2-b332-d85cf385c7b7" id="_110c320b-db48-4ed2-b332-d85cf385c7b7"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
<div><a name="_examples_7" id="_examples_7"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.23.2 Examples</p><div class="example"><a name="_fc2a073f-200b-41c6-9d04-efebf806476c" id="_fc2a073f-200b-41c6-9d04-efebf806476c"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x5927;&#x7FD4; is traditionally pronounced &#x201C;Hiroto&#x201D;, but can also be pronounced as
&#x201C;Haruto&#x201D;, &#x201C;Yamato&#x201D;, &#x201C;Taiga&#x201D;, &#x201C;Sora&#x201D;, &#x201C;Taito&#x201D;, &#x201C;Daito&#x201D;, and
&#x201C;Masato&#x201D;.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_c70f1e56-9f34-41b7-a3a3-3e46011d7685" id="_c70f1e56-9f34-41b7-a3a3-3e46011d7685"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x5927;&#x548C; can be read as Daiwa or Yamato.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_b038ff61-e7da-4eab-9655-6e96dc66e4d4" id="_b038ff61-e7da-4eab-9655-6e96dc66e4d4"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  3</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x6771;&#x6D77;&#x6797; can be read as T&#x14D;kairin or Sh&#x14D;ji.</p></div>
<div class="example"><a name="_8cf2c0aa-b3c4-40e6-91d4-aac007d0d5e3" id="_8cf2c0aa-b3c4-40e6-91d4-aac007d0d5e3"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  4</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span>&#x201C;&#x4E2D;&#x5C71;&#x6A35;&#x201D; (Nakayama Sho), the Japanese pseudonym of
&#x201C;Sun Yat-sen&#x201D;:</p><p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.34</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_9f2cd782-4380-4583-b4b6-46a45ffa69c2" id="_9f2cd782-4380-4583-b4b6-46a45ffa69c2"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">&#x4E2D;&#x5C71;</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">&#x6A35;</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div></div>
<div><a name="_japanese_immigrants_in_brazil" id="_japanese_immigrants_in_brazil"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.23.3 Japanese immigrants in Brazil</p><div class="example"><a name="_9fa5fa6f-5b53-4510-8c4e-c4bfd3e95ac1" id="_9fa5fa6f-5b53-4510-8c4e-c4bfd3e95ac1"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  1</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></p>
  <p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.35</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_c071f06d-a2c0-4c6e-a497-0f0fdbe16b61" id="_c071f06d-a2c0-4c6e-a497-0f0fdbe16b61"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Akemi</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Denise</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Sameshima</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
<div class="example"><a name="_00a16f20-0fd7-41f9-adce-97077ddd2b04" id="_00a16f20-0fd7-41f9-adce-97077ddd2b04"></a><p class="example"><span class="example_label">EXAMPLE  2</span><span style="mso-tab-count:1">&#xA0; </span></p>
  <p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.36</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_0137535f-6e19-42e6-801f-4b421301e3d6" id="_0137535f-6e19-42e6-801f-4b421301e3d6"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Yuri</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Vanessa</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.0pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.0pt;">Ohara</td></tr><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:none;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div></div></div>
        <div><a name="_jewish" id="_jewish"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.24 Jewish</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_5decf275-f4e2-47f2-8d8f-17d75c6cea15" id="_5decf275-f4e2-47f2-8d8f-17d75c6cea15"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo30;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo30;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpMiddle">
    given name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo30;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    patronymic name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_52f118f0-693c-44c0-991c-cf0303ad0751" id="_52f118f0-693c-44c0-991c-cf0303ad0751"></a>Modern Jewish names include Hebrew patronymic names as well as family names.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_8" id="_typical_name_patterns_8"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.24.1 Typical name patterns</p><p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.37</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_43033956-b243-422c-9f8d-f0b9dde433bc" id="_43033956-b243-422c-9f8d-f0b9dde433bc"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">patronymic name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.38</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_5941fc80-fb7a-4fed-aad7-e35a2a2e60da" id="_5941fc80-fb7a-4fed-aad7-e35a2a2e60da"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td></tr></tbody></table></div></div>
<div><a name="_examples_8" id="_examples_8"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.24.2 Examples</p>

</div></div>
        <div><a name="_korean" id="_korean"></a><p class="h2Annex">C.25 Korean</p><p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_bc9e5eb5-72e7-4a47-9a41-02ba0dd6134b" id="_bc9e5eb5-72e7-4a47-9a41-02ba0dd6134b"></a>name components:</p>

  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo31;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpFirst">
    family name
  </p>
  <p style="mso-list:l3 level1 lfo31;" class="MsoListParagraphCxSpLast">
    given name
  </p>

<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_98ee9e2b-5182-422d-a5a9-ec7d89cce623" id="_98ee9e2b-5182-422d-a5a9-ec7d89cce623"></a>A Korean name consists of a family name followed by a given name, as used by
the Korean people in both South Korea and North Korea.</p>
<p class="MsoNormal"><a name="_88b181d1-6163-4433-a0b8-620dd7b0a517" id="_88b181d1-6163-4433-a0b8-620dd7b0a517"></a>In the Korean language,
ireum or seongmyeong usually refers to the family name (seong) and given name
(myeong) together.</p>
<div><a name="_typical_name_patterns_9" id="_typical_name_patterns_9"></a><p class="h3Annex">C.25.1 Typical name patterns</p>

  <p class="TableTitle" style="text-align:center;">Table C.39</p><div align="center"><table class="MsoISOTable" style="mso-table-lspace:15.0cm;margin-left:423.0pt;mso-table-rspace:15.0cm;margin-right:423.0pt;mso-table-bspace:14.2pt;mso-table-anchor-vertical:paragraph;mso-table-anchor-horizontal:column;mso-table-overlap:never;border-spacing:0;border-width:1px;" summary=""><a name="_e3b91eef-cbfd-4685-b2ac-e13f5379f854" id="_e3b91eef-cbfd-4685-b2ac-e13f5379f854"></a><tbody><tr><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">family name</td><td align="left" style="border-top:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-top-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;border-bottom:solid windowtext 1.5pt;mso-border-bottom-alt:solid windowtext 1.5pt;">given name</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>
